    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1277">

                <pb facs="1018" n="902" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg902"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.1123/7.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-24T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1912—12 noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Now that the insurrection has collapsed, do you still wish me to communicate to
                    the Mexican Government the position of the United States regarding closure ports
                    in accordance with instructions in your October 23, 1 p.m.?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
